# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads.
#
# This file exists because of a failure that is hard to read from the error:
# without a .gcloudignore, gcloud filters the upload using .gitignore. This
# repository's .gitignore blocks *.json to keep service account keys out, so the
# npm lockfile never reached Cloud Build and the image failed at
# `COPY web/package-lock.json` with "file does not exist" -- while the identical
# `docker build` succeeded locally, because Docker reads .dockerignore instead.
#
# Keep this in step with .dockerignore. The rules are the same intent: upload the
# source that gets built, and nothing that gets reinstalled or refetched.

# Rebuilt inside the image from the lockfiles
venv/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.coverage
**/.coverage
web/node_modules/
node_modules/
web/dist/

# Fetched fresh, for Linux, in its own build stage
.tools/

# Credentials never leave the machine
.env
*.pem
*.key

.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Not build inputs
infra/
docs/
*.md
LICENSE
